    "minN": 150,
    "maxSeconds": 40,
    "cellTotal": 10000,
    "note": "Seconds the offense lets run before the snap when the game clock is running. Measured 2022-2023: game clock at the previous snap minus that play's measured duration minus the game clock at this snap; nflverse play_clock is 0 on every row 2016-2025, so it cannot be used (DECISIONS.md). restart: the previous snap went out of bounds (1) or drew a flag (2), so the clock was stopped and restarted on the ready signal (designed bin, added after the first in-sample game run showed run-off after such plays is about 4 s shorter and the pooled cells cut run-off after ordinary plays by 2-3 s). toCalled: a timeout is called in this dead ball; the run-off is then the time that runs before the timeout (post-validation revision 2 of step 5). Levels keep score3 down to the third level (revision 3). Step 5c milestone F: a late-only level (time5, lateS3, toCalled) before the score-free level, so a late leader without its own cell no longer pools with trailing teams."
  },
